extends layout

block content
  .page-heading
    div
      .eyebrow STATEMENT IMPORTS
      h1 More history. One budget.
      p Bring your P&N accounts into the picture.
  p Upload one or more OFX exports. Statements you've imported before are recognised automatically, and only new transactions are added. Overlapping exports are fine.
  .alert.alert-info
    | First time for an account? Start with the oldest history you want to keep. To add to an Actual account that already has history, select it and choose the date to import from. Loans usually belong off-budget, and money owed should be negative.
  form#ofx-upload.upload-zone
    +icon('import')
    h2 Start with your statements
    p Choose your OFX or QFX exports. You’ll review accounts and balances before importing.
    label.form-label(for='ofx-files') OFX files (up to 10 files, 5 MB each; 8 MB total)
    input#ofx-files.form-control(type='file' accept='.ofx,.qfx' multiple required)
    button.btn.btn-primary.mt-3(type='submit') Preview files
  #ofx-status.mt-3(role='status' aria-live='polite')
  form#ofx-confirm.mt-4(hidden)
    #ofx-accounts
    p Matching uses shared P&N references. For Up transfers, choose any linked Up account or limit matching to one account. Only unique matches with a bank-identifying description are linked automatically; others remain for review. Existing linked transfers are reused. Future Up syncs also check for matches.
    p Existing accounts keep their opening balance and budget status. New accounts get an opening balance calculated from the statement.
    button#ofx-import.btn.btn-success(type='submit') Import
  #ofx-result.mt-4

block scripts
  script(src='/ofx.js')
